   "shape_m": "p",
   "html_text": "This background picture has been widely discussed and criticized. Leuridan (2012) argues that this view of levels is incoherent, perhaps presupposing the idea of part-hood it should explicate. Potochnik and McGill (2012) argue that the concept of level mischaracterizes the messy relations found in science and insists on a homogeneous composition of things at a single level (though arguably this is not true of mechanistic levels). di Frisco (2017) argues against mechanistic conceptions of levels,",
   "md_text": "This background picture has been widely discussed and criticized. Leuridan (2012) argues that this view of levels is incoherent, perhaps presupposing the idea of part-hood it should explicate. Potochnik and McGill (2012) argue that the concept of level mischaracterizes the messy relations found in science and insists on a homogeneous composition of things at a single level (though arguably this is not true of mechanistic levels). di Frisco (2017) argues against mechanistic conceptions of levels,"
